The bug is in the function returned by `pullFromCache`, inside `GroupByQueryQueryToolChest.getCacheStrategy`, at `processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/groupby/GroupByQueryQueryToolChest.java:653-659`.

```java
int postPos = 0;
while (postItr.hasNext() && results.hasNext()) {
  resultRow.set(postAggregatorStart + postPos, results.next());
}
```

- **Cause:** `postPos` is never incremented, and `postItr.next()` is never called. Every cached post-aggregator value is written into the first post-aggregator slot.
- **Symptom:** This matches the issue. `a2` ends up holding the last value (31,548) and `a3` stays `NULL`. With zero or one post-aggregator the bug doesn't show.
- **Fix:** Inside the loop, call `postItr.next()` and increment `postPos` after each `set`.

`prepareForCache` in the same method writes all the post-aggregator values in order, so it doesn't appear to need a change. I found this by reading the code; I didn't run or edit anything.

